Aim

To create an Amazon S3 bucket, upload an object, and enable public access to the uploaded file using bucket-level and object-level permissions.

Procedure
Step 1: Open Amazon S3
Login to Amazon Web Services AWS Management Console.
Go to:
Services → S3
Click Create Bucket.
Step 2: Configure Bucket

Enter Bucket Name:

my-public-bucket-123
Choose nearest AWS region.
Step 3: Disable Block Public Access
Under Block Public Access settings:
Uncheck Block all public access
Acknowledge warning.
Click Create Bucket.
Step 4: Enable Bucket-Level Public Access
Open created bucket.
Go to:
Permissions tab
Scroll to:
Access Control List (ACL)
Click Edit.
Under Public Access:
Enable:
Everyone (public access) → Read
Save changes.
Step 5: Upload Object
Open:
Objects tab
Click Upload.
Click Add Files.
Select file.
Click Upload.
Step 6: Enable Object-Level Public Access
Open uploaded object.
Go to:
Permissions
Scroll to:
Access Control List (ACL)
Click Edit.
Enable:
Everyone (public access) → Read
Save changes.
Step 7: Verify Public Access
Copy object URL.
Open URL in browser/incognito mode.
Verify file opens without AWS login.
Observation
S3 bucket created successfully.
Public access permissions enabled.
File uploaded successfully.
Uploaded object became publicly accessible through URL.
Result

Successfully created an S3 bucket, uploaded an object, and enabled public access using ACL permissions.
